    "body": "> I think these three PRs would be good to merge before merging into the HTML standard:\r\n> \r\n> * [Remove custom element state when is attribute is blocked WICG/sanitizer-api#396](https://github.com/WICG/sanitizer-api/pull/396)\r\n> * [Clarify condition by splitting it up into explicitly named bools. WICG/sanitizer-api#385](https://github.com/WICG/sanitizer-api/pull/385)\r\n> * [Replace `replace all` with steps from `replaceWith`. WICG/sanitizer-api#375](https://github.com/WICG/sanitizer-api/pull/375)\r\n\r\nSince some security sensitive changes rely on \"sanitizing while parsing\", and that in turn relies on the current post-processing sanitizer being upstreamed, I don't think we should delay upstreaming any further. \r\n\r\nCan we race it? If any of these go in before the upstream PR is in I'll incorporate them into the HTML PR.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
